# Code owners — review-request signal for sensitive paths.
#
# NOTE on enforcement (ADR-062): main's branch protection requires STATUS CHECKS, not reviews — a global
# required-review rule would block the tenant-claims automerge path (GitHub cannot require reviews
# per-path). So entries here REQUEST review; the hard guarantees are:
#   - tenant claims: the Tenant Claims Gate (schema/envelope/quota/path checks) + Kyverno envelope
#     enforcement at admission — deliberately NOT review-gated, that's what makes self-service automerge
#     safe (claims are bounded by the Team envelope, so per-tenant approval is delegated to CI).
#   - Team objects & scaffolder templates: the gate FAILS scaffolder-authored PRs touching these paths
#     until an admin approves the current commit (machine-enforced human review, ADR-062 §1).
#   - everything else: the collaborator set (who can push/merge at all) is the actual control.

# Team objects GRANT envelopes (ADR-062 §1: New Team is human-review, never automerge).
/gitops/teams/           @gangster

# Platform agents (ADR-082): an XAgent claim grants cluster-wide read + a Bedrock grant on the hub, so authoring
# one is admin-gated — the human-review counterpart to the Kyverno restrict-agent-control-plane admission policy.
/gitops/agents/          @gangster

# The People roster (ADR-068 / identity strategy §2.4, #886): a Person grants access, so it's human-reviewed.
# The HARD gate is the People Gate's "People Approval" required check — content-routed (team-lead for team
# grants, access-admin for platform grants/offboarding). This entry is the review-request signal.
/gitops/people/          @gangster

# The workforce role catalog (identity strategy §2.2 / §3.6, #887): changing a role re-permissions everyone who
# holds it (the highest-blast-radius change), so it's admin-gated. The HARD gate is the Roles Gate's "Roles
# Approval" required check (two-person control / meta-governance). This entry is the review-request signal.
/gitops/roles/           @gangster

# Scaffolder templates: a template defines what a self-service portal run can author (and what can
# auto-merge), so template changes are platform-only — same review bar as the sensitive infra paths.
/scaffolder/             @gangster

# CI workflows and the tenant-claims gate scripts: the gate judges automerge, so changes here deserve
# eyes (signal only — see the note above; pull_request_target already prevents a PR from editing the
# gate that evaluates it).
/.github/                @gangster

# Gated prod (#377 / ADR-067 §8 / ADR-068 §7): a prod release digest bump is the one promotion that requires
# human review. The HARD gate is the gitops Gate's "gitops Approval" required check — an APPROVED review (≠ author)
# from the registry-sourced release-approver set (Product.spec.roles.releaseApprover else Team's; #501). This
# entry is the review-request signal; the authoritative approver list lives in gitops/teams + gitops/products.
/gitops/releases/**/prod.yaml      @gangster
/gitops/releases/**/*-prod.yaml    @gangster
